BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Lovers Speed Friending
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T153000
UID:6aa048e93b6c71003e5e85b2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you looking to expand your circle of book loving friends?
  Join us for an afternoon of speedy discussion to make new friends at the 
 library! Whether you are a fan of the classics\, love the excitement of a 
 thriller\, or prefer literary fiction\, this event is a great opportunity 
 to make connections with people who have a shared love of reading.\nTea an
 d cookies will be served.\nSpaces are limited\, so please register to guar
 antee a spot.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on
  this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Lib
 raries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only
  be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Que
 stions about how the library handles your information can be directed to A
 nswerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\
 , Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Parliament Street
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa048e93b6c71003e5e85b2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Série Portraits et autoportraits: Quand la représentation social
 e cède la place aux sentiments.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T153000
UID:6aa17bd8607483003825642c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Du Néoclassicisme à l’Académisme\, de David à Ingres\, l
 es commandes de portraits furent souvent le moyen d’affirmer son rang da
 ns la société. Du Romantisme à l’Impressionnisme\, une sensibilité n
 ouvelle se fait jour : l’on pose en communion avec la nature et non plus
  dans la magnificence de sa demeure\, les regards traduisent des sentiment
 s (Renoir) et non plus une volonté de puissance\, les gestes sont spontan
 és (Degas\, Manet) et non plus codifiés. Quant aux artistes\, ils valori
 sent\, dans leurs autoportraits\, l’acte créateur\, l’inspiration (Gi
 rodet\, Delacroix)\, voire les tourments intérieurs (Courbet\, Baudelaire
 ).\nCette conférence vous est proposée par Gilles Genty\, historien de l
 ’art\, en partenariat avec l’\nAlliance française de Toronto\n.\nAcce
 ssibilité:\nLe sous-titrage en direct ou automatique\, l’interprétatio
 n en langue des signes\, les services d’intervenant\, ou les services d
 ’accompagnement sont disponibles sur demande. Veuillez soumettre votre 
 demande au moins deux semaines à l’avance à : tpl.ca/accessibility-eve
 nts\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form
  is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act
 \, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used f
 or event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abo
 ut how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline 
 staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto 
 ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa17bd8607483003825642c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI Tinkerers Show and Tell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T160000
UID:6aadd76cca248a002916df79@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What are people actually building with AI\, not in the news bu
 t in your city\, by your neighbours?\nJoin our Innovator-in-Residence\,\nR
 yan Kelln\n\, and members of the AI Tinkerers and the Human Feedback Foun
 dation communities\, for an afternoon of live demos and projects at the li
 brary. See what local builders are working on\, ask questions\, and get id
 eas for your own experiments. Real projects\, real people\, no product pit
 ches. A window into what's possible when curious people get their hands on
  AI.\nCHANGE: No registration required. Drop-in program.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aadd76cca248a002916df79
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Specialty Coffee: From Your First Brew to Barista for Newcomer Ent
 repreneurs (Everyone Welcome!)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T160000
UID:6ab7dd7d08693b0f7374c38e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to take your love of coffee beyond a cup of cappuccino? T
 hinking about opening your own café or launching a coffee brand? Explore 
 real-world career paths in coffee - from café barista to roaster to coffe
 e entrepreneur. Find your entry point in this industry and learn about wha
 t works\, what doesn’t\, and what to avoid. This introductory workshop w
 ill include a mini-guided tasting experience.\nPresented by Hong Dai\, own
 er of Another Land Coffee\, a specialty coffee shop located in North York\
 , with over 15 years of experience in the specialty coffee and hospitality
  industry.\nThis program is part of TPL Small Business Month.
LOCATION:Victoria Village
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab7dd7d08693b0f7374c38e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
