BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Introduction to Data Visualization & Storytelling
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T153000
UID:6ab542d56074830038293bde@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Participate in an in-person program to learn data visualizatio
 n\, storytelling\, and data literacy\, equipping participants with essenti
 al skills to transform data into compelling visual narratives. You will le
 arn about the most popular data visualization types\, best practices in da
 ta preparation\, and techniques for selecting effective charts. Through ha
 nds-on exercises\, you will practice creating clear\, impactful visualizat
 ions that communicate data insights effectively. This course is ideal for 
 those who want to enhance their data storytelling skills and build a stron
 g foundation in data visualization.\nPrerequisites: Excel Basics Part 1 or
  equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse and keyboard skills are required.
LOCATION:Humberwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab542d56074830038293bde
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Contacts to Connections : The Art of Building a Genuine Netwo
 rk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T141500
UID:6abad37329c3d600332c3e99@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Networking can feel uncomfortable when it is approached as ask
 ing for favors or trying to impress others. This interactive workshop help
 s participants reframe networking as a process of building authentic\, mut
 ually beneficial relationships. By the end of the session\, you will have 
 a clearer approach to networking and the confidence to initiate meaningful
  conversations that support your career goals.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJ
 oining and participating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nThi
 s program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously s
 upported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors
  Fidelity Canada\, Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter and\n
 William and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more information\, please visit\
 ntpl.ca/careercoach
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abad37329c3d600332c3e99
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
