BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Map It": 2
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T200000
UID:6abec94c11bbf300684ab1b2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Your neighbourhood tells a story and the data to prove it alre
 ady exists. In this three-session series\, you will learn to find real civ
 ic data about your community\, plot it on an interactive map\, and turn wh
 at you discover into a powerful advocacy piece. No technical experience ne
 eded. Just curiosity about where you live and a desire to make it better.\
 nArrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minutes after the program for one-on-
 one consultations\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in Residence se
 ries focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28\, join pro
 grams\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technology strategis
 t Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create positive chan
 ge in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation Collection
  Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toront
 o Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\,
  and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regist
 ration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles 
 your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca
 \n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second Floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abec94c11bbf300684ab1b2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:5 Pieces of the AI Puzzle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T151500
UID:6a7240ffc7e02e3d006dd30a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Keith McDonald\, Founder of Toronto's the literac
 yAI project.\nA multi-media\, interactive program demystifying artificial 
 intelligence through an illuminating five-piece puzzle framework. This ses
 sion guides participants toward a better understanding of AI's presence\, 
 clarifies confusion\, and helps attendees navigate living\, working\, and 
 playing alongside it. Crucially\, attendees gain the foundation and agency
  to demand the AI they want. Registration is required. Runs 60- 90 minutes
  with questions.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7240ffc7e02e3d006dd30a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
