BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Kath Jonathan Presents "The Resistance Painter"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T150000
UID:6ac586a5295b3b0033cac783@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Author\, Kath Jonathan presents and discusses the characters\,
  conflicts and family theme of her bestselling novel\, “\nThe Resistance
  Painter\n”. This dual timeline World War II story is set in 1940's Wars
 aw\, Poland and 2010 Toronto\, Canada.\nThe presentation begins with a sho
 rt reading\, then a description of her WWII\, dual timeline novel\, The Re
 sistance Painter\, its main characters\, conflicts\, themes and questions.
  More specifically these include the question which haunts the main female
  characters: How do you live with integrity and compassion in the middle o
 f a war? It’s a question the audience is asked to personally hold in pla
 ce during the presentation for discussion later. The 1940’s Warsaw narra
 tive centers the young painter\, Irena\, who joins the Polish resistance a
 rmy and makes art as a record of war\, and later\, after a terrible wartim
 e betrayal\, continues making art in Toronto as a means of survival.\nDrop
 -In.\nThe Resistance Painter
LOCATION:Victoria Village
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac586a5295b3b0033cac783
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
