BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Gravity Grand Prix
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T190000
UID:6a79f5b6cca66c2f00a98e97@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to design\, build\, and race! This high-speed engine
 ering challenge invites young adults (competing in teams of 2 ages 18-24) 
 to design the ultimate gravity-powered race car. Using professional 3D mod
 eling software and cutting-edge 3D printing technology\, your team will co
 mpete to see who can conquer the downhill track the fastest. The core of t
 his challenge is physics: maximizing kinetic energy while minimizing frict
 ion. How will you transform potential energy into pure speed?🛠️ The C
 hallenge Rules\nThe Software: All cars must be fully designed from scratch
  using OnShape. A brief Introduction to the software will be provided.\nTh
 e Material Limit: To keep the playing field level\, your final race car is
  strictly limited to a maximum of 30 grams of 3D printed filament and 2 to
 oth picks.\nFree Prototyping: Failure is part of engineering! Teams are en
 couraged to print\, test\, and redesign. Prototype prints are completely f
 ree throughout the design phase.\nThe Track: A straight\, downhill gravity
  track built for maximum acceleration.\n📅 Timeline & Important Dates\nD
 esign & Prototyping Week: Nov 4 to Nov 11— Access the DIH\, collaborate 
 with your partner\, and test your prototypes.\nRace Day: Nov 11 (Exactly o
 ne week after design week) — Family and friends are welcome to watch the
  final showdown!\n💡 Key Engineering Focus Areas to take home the trophy
 \, your team will need to think critically about:\nAerodynamics & Friction
 : How will you reduce air resistance and wheel friction to keep your car g
 liding?\nWeight Distribution: How can you strategically place your 30-gram
  limit to maximize downward momentum?
LOCATION:Malvern\, Inside the Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a79f5b6cca66c2f00a98e97
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
