BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bring Your Problem: Can AI Help?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T200000
UID:6a9b519baafa61002961b295@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a recurring problem you think AI might help with? 
 A thing you keep doing by hand that feels like it should be easier? Bring 
 it. If you don't have one\, come help your neighbours with theirs.\nIn thi
 s interactive class with our Innovator-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, you'
 ll learn a simple seven-step way to think about problems: what's annoying 
 you\, what you've tried\, what AI could actually do\, and where it would f
 ail. We'll gather real problems from the room\, sort them into groups\, an
 d map out what's worth solving with AI\, and what's better solved without 
 it. We'll also talk honestly about what an AI fix costs: your money\, your
  time\, and sometimes your private information. The problems AI could help
  with most are often the most personal\, and the most personal ones are wo
 rth the most care.\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\, 20
 26 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of
  the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be fill
 ed on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b519baafa61002961b295
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
