SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Build Your First App with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T200000
UID:6a9b51a71c197d11325d7021@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could build an app just by describing it\, with no
  coding experience needed? That's vibe coding.\nIn this workshop led by ou
 r Innovator-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, you'll use an AI coding assist
 ant to build your own small\, useful webpage\, checklist\, or organizer fr
 om scratch. You'll learn the build loop: describe what you want\, review t
 he plan\, build one feature\, test it\, fix the bugs\, and write documenta
 tion so you (or anyone) can understand it later.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, 
 keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding exper
 ience required.\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\, 2026 
 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of th
 e start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be filled 
 on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf you wis
 h to save your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your own USB
  stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes ac
 tivities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou
  do not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants ar
 e encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, whi
 ch include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the pri
 vacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code
 \nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nL
 earn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn m
 ore about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\
 nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public 
 Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d
 ). The information will only be used for event and program registration\, 
 delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your info
 rmation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-
 397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a71c197d11325d7021
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
