BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Turning Red Flags into Strengths: How to Answer Tough Interview Qu
 estions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T180000
UID:6ab45d7fda318a10e63655ea@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Tough interview questions can make even strong candidates seco
 nd-guess themselves. This practical workshop helps participants identify t
 he experiences that may feel difficult to explain in an interview and lear
 n how to present them with confidence and clarity. Through common intervie
 w scenarios\, participants will practice reframing gaps\, career changes\,
  weaknesses\, and 'lack of canadian experience' into credible stories that
  highlight their strengths\, learning and growth.\nThis program is part of
  TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by our lead
  donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada\, F
 riends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter and\nThe William and Nona
  Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more information\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careerco
 ach\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and participating in a Zoom webinar\
 n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab45d7fda318a10e63655ea
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
