SUMMARY:The Shadow of 999 Queen Street West: Toronto’s Lunatic Asylum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:6ad28387901b02002cc2fce4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Fifty years after its demolition\, the shadow of 999 Queen Str
 eet West still looms large in Toronto. This presentation explores the asyl
 um's origins as a temporary facility within one of Toronto's first gaols\,
  as well as the personalities and politics that brought such a mammoth bui
 lding to life. It will also look at its unique architecture\, its treatmen
 t of patients and its presence as a Victorian tourist attraction.\nPresent
 ed by:\nAndrew Nablo
