BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Run Your One-Person Business with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T180000
UID:6a9b51bb1c197d11325d7089@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When you're the whole company\, the admin never ends: emails\,
  scheduling\, proposals\, follow-ups. What if you could design a system to
  handle the busywork?\nIn this class led by our Innovator-in-Residence\,\n
 Ryan Kelln\n\, you'll learn to design an administrative system for a one-p
 erson business with AI as your assistant: intake pipelines\, email draftin
 g\, client communication\, and scheduling. Learn to map work into four pil
 es: what's rules-based\, what AI drafts\, what needs your judgment\, and w
 hat should never be automated. You'll build reusable templates and leave w
 ith a clearer plan for how AI could help your business.\nPrerequisites: M
 ouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No codin
 g experience required.\nRegistration is required and will start November 9
 \, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minut
 es of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be
  filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf
  you wish to save your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your
  own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program inc
 ludes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library lapto
 ps.\nYou do not need to create your own account for this program.\nPartici
 pants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessio
 ns\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review
  the privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nCla
 ude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\
 nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Antigravity\nLea
 rn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn mor
 e about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
