DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T193000
UID:6aa94f18ab7a8e0037c1e5fb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active parti
 cipant in everyday democracy in this fun\, interactive\n45-minute\nsession
 . Democracy Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by expl
 oring the skills that help people participate in civic life\, build unders
 tanding and work together.\nIn this session\, we’ll exercise our\nEmpath
 y\nmuscles. In a democracy\, we have different perspectives. If we want to
  understand others and be understood\, we must put ourselves in each other
 's shoes.\nThis program is for\nadults\n. Drop ins are welcome.\nThis prog
 ram is offered in partnership with Democracy Fitness Global and MASS LBP.\
 nGenerously supported by McConnell Foundation.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa94f18ab7a8e0037c1e5fb
