BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Screen Scaries: Black Christmas\, Bob Clark (1974)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261228T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261228T200000
UID:6ab5a6473dd190003e746a26@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Get your spook on with this month's scary movie screening of\
 nBlack Christmas\n(1974)\, directed by Bob Clark.\nA prototype of the Ame
 rican slasher\,\nBlack Christmas\nwears its Giallo influences on its sleev
 e and sets a blueprint for genre films like John Carpenter's\nHalloween\n
 (1977). Shot in Toronto\, the film follows a group of sorority girls over 
 their winter break as they are harassed by a series of disturbing phone ca
 lls.\nBlack Christmas\nhas a running time of 1 hour and 37 minutes\, and i
 s rated R.\nThere will be a short introduction to the film followed by the
  screening\, which will be accompanied by closed captions.\nThe next Scree
 n Scaries will be:\nJanuary 25\, 2027:\nRing\n(1998\, Japan) Hideo Nakata.
  Runtime: 1h35m\; Rating: PG
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab5a6473dd190003e746a26
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
